# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time environment variables (Vite only exposes VITE_* to the browser)
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local overrides, and configure the same
# variables in the hosting provider (e.g. Vercel → Project → Environment
# Variables) for production builds.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute URL where the site is deployed. Used for the canonical link and the
# Open Graph / Twitter preview URLs in index.html. When it is left empty those
# tags are omitted, so no broken absolute URLs are ever published.
# Example: VITE_SITE_URL="https://habibur-rahman-portfolio.vercel.app"
VITE_SITE_URL=""

# Optional HTTPS endpoint that receives contact form submissions (Formspree,
# Web3Forms, a Vercel serverless function, a Render API route, ...).
# Leave empty to fall back to the visitor's mail client, which opens with the
# inquiry pre-filled — the form never silently discards a message.
# Example: VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT="https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx"
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=""
